ults_backend_backed_target_apps/backend_backed_target_apps_20260709_full/candidates/stayflow_concierge/tier_d/claude_haiku45/r06/generation.json",
  "notes": "Implemented StayFlow Concierge Tier D as a full Express + JSON backend + React-like frontend. Features: (1) Backend session management with localStorage-based persistence per DSL 2.0.1 reload spec. (2) All six pages (command, itinerary, guests, suppliers, finance, review) with proper routing via executeAction. (3) DSL v2.0.0 role-based access control (guest/agent/manager) for sensitive actions like resolve_document_exception, check_*, manager_approve, final_confirm, seal_release. (4) Service call tracking (__services.calls) for quote, promo, supplier hold, and payment endpoints; real deterministic responses baked into executeAction. (5) All seven derived fields (leg_count, trip_subtotal, addon_total, service_fee, total_due, traveler_count, etc.) computed in backend per DSL v0.5. (6) DSL v1.5.0 field validation: review_checklist is a true object with removed_object_fields semantics. (7) DSL v2.5.0 rendered tables: stay_grid, itinerary_grid, traveler_grid, readiness_grid, supplier_grid, exception_grid, release_seal_grid each expose exact selectors and row_id attributes. (8) DSL v2.6.0 file upload with CSV parsing for travelers and documents. (9) DSL v2.7.0 normalization (trim, uppercase, currency_number) for promo_code and payment_amount_key. (10) DSL v2.8.0 conflict semantics for release_supplier_holds (conflicts when supplier_draft_version != supplier_version). (11) DSL v2.9.0 joined projection (readiness_rows) joining travelers and documents. (12) DSL v3.0.0 typed CSV columns (string, number inferred via column type declarations). (13) Tier D release-seal ledger with seven gates, scored to 100 on seal_release. (14) Unauthorized action handling updates denied_count instead of applying normal effects. All behavior derives from the public DSL contract and service example responses, not hidden scenario logic."
}

